On 2007-12-10, Stathol Turris <stathol@hotmail.com> wrote:
> On Dec 7, 2007, Doug Freyburger wrote:
>> Current bones file processing converts.  Maybe a better mechanism
>> is to delete the object if it collides with an existing artifact or
>> the character's quest artifact - Artifacts are supposed to be unique
>> and held by the dieties and/or the quest nemesis so the one in the
>> bones file just called back by the dieties or retrieved by the
>> nemesis.
> Why not put the cart before the horse? That is, have the game decide
> in advance which bones file, if any, will be linked into the game at
> the beginning. 

Consider the following:

-- A bones file on level 20 is selected for inclusion.
-- That bones file is "locked" so that no other game can load that
level's bones.  Due to the nature of Nethack's bones structure, no other
game can save that level's bones either.

If you want to solve the above problem by unlinking the bones at game
start, consider how many games never make it to DL20; you are
effectively creating a circumstance where deep bones are never found.

If you just leave the bones there until the player reaches those bones,
what about those players who take a week for a single game?  That locks
off an entire level of bones until done; on a public server, this works
out very poorly as suddenly most low levels can no longer leave or load
bones, because all the levels are locked up.

> I think that any way you turn it, bones files are always going to be
> a compromise.

Almost certainly true without some fundamental design changes to the
nature of Nethack itself.

